  "answer": "To get a comprehensive list of apartment buildings opening in 2027, you'll generally need to consult specialized real estate data providers and industry reports, as this type of information is part of ongoing market analysis and development pipelines.\n\n**Key Data Sources and Companies:**\n\n*   **Yardi Matrix / RentCafe**: Yardi Matrix is consistently cited as a primary source for multifamily supply forecasts and construction data. Its sister company, RentCafe, often publishes reports based on this data. They produce detailed reports, such as the \"Multifamily Supply Forecast Bulletin,\" which tracks units under construction and projected completions.\n*   **CoStar / Apartments.com**: CoStar is another leading provider of commercial real estate information, analytics, and news. Apartments.com, powered by CoStar data, also publishes updates on U.S. multifamily construction activity and forecasts. These platforms offer market intelligence tools for real estate professionals.\n*   **LoopNet**: While more of a commercial real estate listing service, LoopNet (owned by CoStar) can be a source for identifying development land and properties for sale, which sometimes includes projects in various stages of planning or construction.\n\n**2027 Apartment Construction Outlook:**\n\nOverall, apartment deliveries are projected to slow down significantly in 2027, potentially reaching a 10-year low. Yardi Matrix anticipates approximately 319,000 to 360,500 new rental units nationwide in 2027. This expected slowdown is largely due to a decrease in construction starts in previous years, coupled with factors like weaker rent growth, high financing costs, and rising development expenses.\n\n**Notable Projects Expected to Open in 2027:**\n\nWhile a complete, exhaustive list would require access to paid subscription databases, several projects have been publicly announced with 2027 completion dates:\n\n*   **Alexan Azalea (Arcadia, CA)**: This seven-story, 319-unit multi-family residential building by Trammell Crow Residential is expected to open in early 2027. It will include 26 affordable units.\n*   **Southernside East (Greenville, SC)**: This project will add 93 affordable apartments specifically for seniors and is anticipated to open in early 2027.\n*   **Southernside West (Greenville, SC)**: Also in Greenville, this development will provide 54 affordable senior apartments and units for individuals with disabilities, with completion expected in October 2027.\n*   **Tanner Road (Greenville, SC)**: Flournoy Development Group is developing this 461-unit multifamily community, slated for completion in March 2027.\n*   **Brownsville Arts Center & Apartments (BACA) (Brooklyn, NY)**: This project will feature 283 affordable rental units, with studios to three-bedroom layouts, and is expected to be completed by December 2027.\n\n**Regional Trends and Areas of Activity:**\n\n*   **New York, Dallas-Fort Worth, and Austin, TX**: These metropolitan areas are projected to continue leading in new apartment construction through 2028, even with a general slowdown anticipated until 2027. New York City, in particular, has a significant construction pipeline.\n*   **Southwest Florida Coast**: This region shows a high percentage (over 15%) of its housing inventory currently under construction.\n*   **Tippecanoe County, Indiana (near Purdue University)**: This area is experiencing rapid growth, with over 500 apartments in various stages of construction and plans for several hundred more multifamily units as part of larger developments like Millbrook.\n\n**Focus on Affordable Housing**:\nThere is an increasing trend towards affordable and partially affordable multifamily projects in the new development mix. Yardi Matrix forecasts a 22% increase in partially affordable units and a 44% increase in fully affordable apartments in 2027 compared to 2020 levels.\n\nTo access detailed lists of specific apartment buildings and projects, subscribing to services like Yardi Matrix or CoStar would be the most effective approach. These platforms offer granular data, including project names, locations, unit counts, and estimated completion dates.",
